Z||000000||DreXteR||01-26-2001||02:51 PM||||Well, I decided to make the 3.4TDC swap. Now I will check for prices and stuff.<P>I have a 86GT 4Speed. What 3.4TDC I need for my car? I read that an engine came out from an auto cant work with manual. And what other stuff is needed from the 3.4 to make the swap. <P>Does somebody know how much this swap will cost? <P>BTW, I will need the help of this forum to achieve the goal.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><BR>Thanx everyone<P>DreXteR||||reg||5
Z||000001||Old Lar||01-26-2001||03:36 PM||||Cost will depend on whether you do the labor yourself and where you get your engine from.<P>Twin Lakes Fiero and the Fiero Factory do new crate engine replacements for $4-5K.  That is a new engine.  Twin Lakes uses new injectors, water pump, starter, and I think A/C conversion to 134a included.<P>Costs will vary for swaping a used engine.  Other components may be required once the car is out of the engine.<P>||||reg||3
Z||000002||DreXteR||01-26-2001||04:07 PM||||Im in Puerto Rico. A friend of mine have some contacts with a store that deals with used engines, maybe the can give me a 3.4 from a Z34 but I need the year and other stuff for let them know what is needed.<P>Thanx||||reg||1
Z||000003||fierosound||01-26-2001||05:13 PM||||Several people have already done that.  See this website on what's involved.   I decided to go with a performace built 3.4L pushrod engine instead...<P> <A HREF="http://www.pelkie.com/fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.pelkie.com/fiero.htm</A> ||||reg||10
Z||000004||DreXteR||01-28-2001||12:46 PM||||But I need to know what year of a Z34 is needed for my 86GT 4speed. And if an engine from an auto will work with my 4speed manual.<P>Thanx<P>||||reg||4
Z||000005||Philphine||01-28-2001||01:13 PM||||i think of all the engines we talk about and consider the 3.4 tdc is about the only one that could be had with a manual tranny (maybe some v8's?). it makes me think it's a good swap because beside seeming like a nice engine, it might be easier to get around the flywheel and computer issues. but thats a guess on my part. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||mrfiero||01-28-2001||01:43 PM||||Look for '93-'97 (I think) Lumima Z-34's.  Most were autos, but there were a few 5-speeds (Getrag 284).  I have found one in a junkyard, but it was hit hard on the left front and I don't think it will come out easily.  It also has a digital dash, so I could not tell what mileage it had.  I forgot to see what tranny it had too (probably an auto.).<P>An auto engine will work with a manual, but you will need the ECM from a manual or customize the ECM from the auto.  Don't ask me what modifications to do.....I have no idea.<P>I wish I could help you more. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||fierosound||01-28-2001||02:22 PM||||This site list which cars had the 3.4L DOHC engine  <A HREF="http://members.aol.com/KWZ26/models.html" TARGET=_blank>http://members.aol.com/KWZ26/models.html</A> <P>This is a discussion forum for DOHC owners  <A HREF="http://angelfire.com/ca2/34Performance/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://angelfire.com/ca2/34Performance/index.html</A> ||||reg||10
Z||000008||87GTZ34||01-28-2001||10:46 PM||||If anyone is interested, I ran across a '92 Lumina Z34 this past WE at the upickit.  Eng & trans (4spd auto) was in tact.  That yard lets them go for $150 although you would probably want to consider a rebuild.  A good candidate for TDC project car.||||reg||1
Z||000009||DreXteR||01-29-2001||09:48 AM||||Thanx, I will try to reach one Z34 in Puerto Rico. <P>Btw, if only I can find an engine with an auto, Where can be possible get the manual ecm or who make the mods for the auto?<P>Thanx  Again   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>DreX<P>PS Look @ my baby! I die to see it runinig again.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR> <IMG SRC="http://users.centennialpr.net/drexter/Fiero/fiero1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||tgowens||01-29-2001||11:48 AM||||the engine to get is the 3.4L pushrod engine from a '93 to '95 Camaro or Firebird - this is the easiest swap..........you will need to reposition the starter to the other side of the engine. It will bolt up to the 4-speed tranny easily. and you will not need to change the wiring harness or ECM. Everything from the heads up from your 2.8 will bolt onto the 3.4..........this is the Rear Wheel Drive version engine, not to be confused with the other 3.4's from the Front Wheel Drive vehicles!<P>This is the easiest swap, the other 3.4's, dual cams etc. are much more difficult to swap in..........||||reg||1
Z||000011||DreXteR||01-29-2001||01:26 PM||||I know that the pushrod is the easy swap, but not have the power like the tdc.<P>Thats why im going with it. BTW, how much power i can obtain from pushrod?<P>DreX||||reg||1
